    "# Sprint 0: Data Review and Group Work Primer\n",
    "\n",
    "## Brief\n",
    "\n",
    "- Find a data set regarding our selection of topic for Sprint 0.\n",
    "- Find code using websites and other resources to manipulate our data points.\n",
    "- Massage our data to fit said code.\n",
    "- Decide on a programming environment R/Python.\n",
    "- Create a comprehensive report logically ordering our work.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Our Project\n",
    "\n",
    "We used the Brier score to show which of our five chosen bookmakers predicted the winner of each English Premier League game most accurately; through the seasons 21-22, 22-23, 23-24.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Brier score calculates this using the following equation:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "BS=\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{t=1}^{N}(f_t-\\sigma_t)^2\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Essentially this equation takes the predicted probability $f_t$ and the observed binary outcome $\\sigma_t$:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\sigma_t =\n",
    "\\begin{cases}\n",
    "0\\\\\n",
    "1\n",
    "\\end{cases}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "giving an outcome between $0$ and $1$, where the closer $BS$ is to $0$, the more accurate the prediction.\n",
    "\n",
    "We used each of the bookmakers odds and took the reciprocal in order to find the probability for each outcome they predicted (home win, draw, away win).\n",
    "\n",
    "## Team\n",
